# System lines meeting an open question: a background agent's report
# (serve's {"notice"} line), a watcher's wake and the page's model/effort
# commands, arriving while the parent session is blocked on tools.ask or
# tools.secret. Recipe: go/tests/model/README.md. ask_answer.fizz covers
# the person's own POSTs; background_agents.fizz never has the parent
# blocked on a question. This spec is where the two meet.
#
# One stdin pipe carries every line serve writes into a child, and the
# child's stdin pump (plugins/ui/headless.go hlLineIn) is what decides
# what a line is. Four writers:
#   Notify     notify.go notifyFrom, called by children.go report when a
#              background agent's turn closes: writes {"notice": text}
#              raw, NOT through Send, so no pending-ask refusal (the
#              notice is meant to get past an open ask).
#   Wake       watchers.go supWaker.Wake -> Send: refused while an ask is
#              armed. watch.go deliver checks Idle (status not running or
#              needs-you) first, then Wakes; the queue was cleared before
#              the Wake, and a refused wake is not requeued.
#   SetModel / SetEffort   supervisor.go -> Send("/model x" | "/think x"):
#              refused while armed (the page gets the error, meta keeps
#              the old model).
#   Answer     supervisor.go Answer: the person's text, raw, then disarm.
#
# A write and the child's read of it are one step here (as in
# ask_answer.fizz): the pump reads a line as soon as it is written. The
# window where a line written before an ask is read after it opened (the
# pump held up in hlNotice's 30 s wait or hlSubmit's reload wait) is not
# modelled; see the finding below.
#
# Fields:
#   status   running | needs-you | done  (the row, StatusOf)
#   ask      "" | plain | secret: the question open in the child, which
#            serve has armed (write+read being one step, arm == open)
#   plainAsked, secretAsked   each question is asked at most once, so the
#            graph stays finite
#   notice   none | queued | delivered: the one background report. queued
#            = in job-notices, waiting for the loop's next step (an open
#            ask blocks that step); delivered = the loop handed it to the
#            model. noticeCount counts deliveries.
#   wake     none | queued | checked | delivered | dropped: the one
#            watcher wake. checked = deliver() found the session idle and
#            is about to Send.
#   model    none | applied | refused: the last /model the page sent.
#   secret   "" | person | notice | phantom: what tools.secret stored
#            (secretVia trims and stores whatever answered its ask).
#   noticeAnswered   a notice line was taken as an ask's answer (sticky).
#   phantom          a line that was not a report was queued as a notice
#                    (sticky): the person's plain answer that happens to
#                    parse as {"notice": ...}.
#   strayLine        serve wrote a wake or command line while an ask was
#                    armed (sticky): it would have been read as the answer.
#
# Where this disagrees with the code as of main 5471918e, the spec says
# what the flow promises and the code is the finding:
#   - A pending SECRET takes the raw line before the notice sniff
#     (headless.go:369-377). A background agent finishing while its
#     parent has tools.secret open: the {"notice": ...} line is stored as
#     the secret (keychain, ref in project.yml), the secret ask closes as
#     if answered, and the report is never delivered. Here Notify routes
#     the notice first whatever ask is open (NoticeNeverAnswers,
#     OnlySecretIsTheAnswer, NoticeExactlyOnce, NoticeDelivered fail on
#     the product's order).
#   - A plain answer is written raw and sniffed as JSON (headless.go:
#     381-392): an answer whose text is {"notice": "..."} becomes a
#     phantom notice, the ask stays open in the child while serve has
#     disarmed it, and the next /prompt (no longer refused) is eaten as
#     the answer. Here AnswerNoticeLike answers the question.

role Session:
    action Init:
        self.status = "running"
        self.ask = ""
        self.plainAsked = False
        self.secretAsked = False
        self.notice = "none"
        self.noticeCount = 0
        self.wake = "none"
        self.model = "none"
        self.secret = ""
        self.noticeAnswered = False
        self.phantom = False
        self.strayLine = False

    # The model calls tools.ask / tools.secret: the child emits kind
    # "ask" and serve arms it (emitLocked); the row turns needs-you. Asks
    # never overlap: a block blocks on its ask.
    atomic action AskPlain:
        require self.status == "running" and self.ask == "" and not self.plainAsked
        self.plainAsked = True
        self.ask = "plain"
        self.status = "needs-you"

    atomic action AskSecret:
        require self.status == "running" and self.ask == "" and not self.secretAsked
        self.secretAsked = True
        self.ask = "secret"
        self.status = "needs-you"

    # A background agent's turn closes and serve reports it
    # (childEventLocked -> report -> notifyFrom): the {"notice"} line is
    # written whatever is armed, and the child routes it to job-notices
    # before any answer handling. It never touches the ask or the arm.
    atomic action Notify:
        require self.notice == "none"
        self.notice = "queued"

    # job-notices hands the report to the loop: before the next model
    # step of a running turn, or by waking an idle agent. A turn blocked
    # on an ask takes no step until the ask returns.
    atomic fair action DeliverNotice:
        require self.notice == "queued" and self.ask == ""
        self.notice = "delivered"
        self.noticeCount += 1
        if self.status == "done":
            self.status = "running"

    # A watcher's check produced news: queued in the watch engine.
    atomic action WatcherQueue:
        require self.wake == "none"
        self.wake = "queued"

    # deliver(): Idle reads the derived status; a session running or
    # needing you keeps its queue.
    atomic fair action WatcherCheck:
        require self.wake == "queued" and self.status == "done"
        self.wake = "checked"

    # ...then Wake -> Send. Send refuses on an armed ask (the ask may have
    # opened since the check: the person prompted in between). The queue
    # was already cleared, so a refused wake is gone.
    atomic fair action WatcherSend:
        require self.wake == "checked"
        if self.ask != "":
            self.wake = "dropped"
        else:
            self.writeStray()
            self.wake = "delivered"
            # Steers a running turn, or starts one on an idle session.
            self.status = "running"

    # The page's model picker (and the effort picker, the same Send of a
    # slash command): 409 while an ask is armed, else dispatched by the
    # child without reaching the model.
    atomic action SetModel:
        require self.model != "applied"
        if self.ask != "":
            self.model = "refused"
        else:
            self.writeStray()
            self.model = "applied"

    # The person answers from the page (Answer): the line goes to the
    # open question, serve disarms. A secret stores exactly that text.
    atomic action Answer:
        require self.ask != ""
        if self.ask == "secret":
            self.secret = "person"
        self.closeAsk()

    # The same with a plain answer whose text parses as {"notice": ...}:
    # it is still the person's answer.
    atomic action AnswerNoticeLike:
        require self.ask == "plain"
        self.closeAsk()

    # The ask times out (Asker): the call returns with no answer, serve
    # disarms on its result/call end. A secret stores nothing.
    atomic fair action Timeout:
        require self.ask != ""
        self.closeAsk()

    atomic fair action Finish:
        require self.status == "running" and self.ask == ""
        self.status = "done"

    # The person prompts an idle session: a new turn.
    atomic action Prompt:
        require self.status == "done"
        self.status = "running"

    atomic func closeAsk():
        self.ask = ""
        self.status = "running"

    # A wake or command line written into stdin: only ever with nothing
    # armed. Kept as a func so a mutation that drops Send's refusal is
    # one line.
    atomic func writeStray():
        if self.ask != "":
            self.strayLine = True

action Init:
    session = Session()

# A {"notice"} line is never an answer to any ask, plain or secret.
always assertion NoticeNeverAnswers:
    return not session.noticeAnswered

# Nothing but the person's answer is ever stored as a secret.
always assertion OnlySecretIsTheAnswer:
    return session.secret == "" or session.secret == "person"

# Only a finished agent's report is ever queued as a notice.
always assertion NoPhantomNotice:
    return not session.phantom

# Serve writes no line but the answer and notices while an ask is armed.
always assertion NoStrayLineWhileArmed:
    return not session.strayLine

# A notice is delivered exactly once, whether or not an ask was open.
always assertion NoticeExactlyOnce:
    return session.noticeCount <= 1 and (session.notice == "delivered") == (session.noticeCount == 1)

# needs-you is exactly an open question.
always assertion NeedsYouIsTheAsk:
    return (session.status == "needs-you") == (session.ask != "")

# A notice sent while an ask is open reaches the parent's loop: the ask
# ends (answer, or the fair timeout) and the loop's next step takes it.
always eventually assertion NoticeDelivered:
    return session.notice != "queued"

# An open question, the secret included, stays until the person answers
# or it times out; with the timeout fair, it does end.
always eventually assertion AskEnds:
    return session.ask == ""
